## 🧩 1. Overview

This project demonstrates a simple end-to-end DBT workflow using Snowflake:

Ingest raw data into Snowflake

Transform data using DBT models

Create staging + mart layers

Auto-generate schemas & DAG

Run models

Test models

The project contains:

✔ 1 raw table
✔ 1 staging model
✔ 1 mart model
✔ dbt_project.yml
✔ profiles.yml instructions
✔ full documentation

## 🧑‍💻 2. Prerequisites

Snowflake account (UI access is enough)

VS Code

Python 3.8+

Git installed

dbt-core + dbt-snowflake

## ❄️ 3. Snowflake Setup (Already Done by You)

Run in Snowflake:

CREATE OR REPLACE DATABASE DEMO_DB;
CREATE OR REPLACE SCHEMA RAW;

CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE RAW.RAW_SALES (
    order_id INTEGER,
    customer_name STRING,
    amount NUMBER(10,2),
    order_date DATE
);

INSERT INTO RAW.RAW_SALES VALUES
(1, 'RAMESH', 120, '2024-01-10'),
(2, 'SURESH', 250, '2024-01-11'),
(3, 'MAHESH', 450, '2024-01-12'),
(4, 'RAMESH', 300, '2024-02-01');

## ⚙️ 4. Install DBT

Run in VS Code Terminal:

pip install dbt-core dbt-snowflake


Verify:

dbt --version

## 🏗️ 5. Create DBT Project (Step 1)

Run:

dbt init my_first_project

## 📝 PROMPTS & PARAMETERS DURING dbt init (Step 2)

Below are the exact values you should enter during initialization:

Prompt	Value to Enter
Which database?	1 (Snowflake)
account	<your_account>.your_region>
Example: xy12345.us-east-1
user	Your Snowflake username
password	Your Snowflake password
role	SYSADMIN (or your role)
warehouse	COMPUTE_WH
database	DEMO_DB
schema	DBT_DEV
threads	4
client_session_keep_alive	False
## 🔧 6. Configure profiles.yml

Create file:

C:\Users\<your_user>\.dbt\profiles.yml


Paste:

my_first_project:
  target: dev
  outputs:
    dev:
      type: snowflake
      account: <your_account>              # Example: xy12345.us-east-1
      user: <your_username>
      password: <your_password>
      role: SYSADMIN
      warehouse: COMPUTE_WH
      database: DEMO_DB
      schema: DBT_DEV
      threads: 4
      client_session_keep_alive: False


Test connection:

dbt debug

